w: I'm but a stran- ger here, Heav'n is my home;
w: What though the temp- est rage, Heav'n is my home;
w: There at my Sa- vior's side Heav'n is my home;
w: There- fore I mur- mur not, Heav'n is my home;
D2 B B | B A d2 | A2 F E | D4 |
w: Earth is a des- ert drear, Heav'n is my home.
w: Short is my pil- grim- age, Heav'n is my home;
w: I shall be glor- i- fied, Heav'n is my home.
w: What- e'er my earth- ly lot, Heav'n is my home;
